                <pb facs="0895" n="779" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg779"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/3150: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Harbin</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hanson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-08-02T16:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">August 2,
                                1923—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 2—1:15
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>On August 1 General Chang Huan-hsiang attempted to take over land department of
                    Chinese Eastern Railway but met with opposition and protest on the part of
                    railway officials and representative of Russo-Asiatic Bank. Chinese officials
                    now apparently weakening in their aggressive attitude and endeavoring to find
                    satisfactory retreat from difficulties within which they involved themselves.
                    Legation has been notified.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
